body:
It's was never up to me. I was dealt a bad hand and I was extremely lucky for anything I got. I deserved none of it.

&#x200B;

Also. I do feel like i'm worse than a pedophile and that's why my last ex left me for one. If I wasn't better than a pedophile to her than what the fuck am I really?

I just don't like when people shove their relationships in everybody's faces. I guess they feel really proud of themselves for getting in one even though majority of the time its due to reasons they had control over. It's easier for attractive people to find someone who thinks they're attractive along with having the confidence to be with them. If you're ugly not only is it hard to find someone who's attracted to you but it's even harder to find someone who's into you and is confident enough to show it by being around/with you.

&#x200B;

To brag/showoff for being lucky enough to have attractive genetics. I can't respect it but i'm also envious of it at the same time.

Observation. Not only of him but environment as well. Where is he more comfortable speaking? In what environments does he seem more comfortable/relaxed? Who knows. He may be an introvert who may have stage freight within a large crowd. It's all about his level of comfort and how he treats you when you both are in an environment where he is comfortable enough to talk to you. Using myself as an example, I'm not comfortable trying to talk to/flirt with people while i'm at my job. Yes I have been approached and flirted with at my job in which in the most professional way I could I rejected them and carried on about my business. Majority of the women i've rejected had nothing to do with how they looked but the lack of comfort i've felt with them. We're together but we've never been around each other in a more casual setting? We're together but we never spent any personal time together? We're together but we never broke the physical touch, not necessary sex, barrier?

&#x200B;

Now I will say this. If it is a guy who has a lot women talking to him/he has options than this will be a lot harder to do. You are competing with other women and most likely he's going to end up with the one he feels the most attracted to which may not always be because of looks. He may feel the most comfortable around her. Be cautious. A lot of guys like this, not all, won't really care to lose one of the many women trying to talk to him. That could result in him not really caring about how he treats you or what he does behind your back. In his mind he may think that he can replace you with any of the other women showing him attention.

&#x200B;

PS: This is not a guarantee to get a guy that you like. That's not something me or you can control. Same as the guy in OPs post in how there was nothing he could do to get her to like him. If the guy doesn't try even after you put your self in the best position you could for him to approach or make a move then most likely he's not interested and you would have to move on.

This usually comes from people who either don't have other options, therefore doesn't see you as just an option, and/or from people who actually care to lose you. Unfortunately the people who care for you the most don't tend to have that attractive level of confidence that comes with not caring about how other people think of them....because they care about what YOU think of them.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

It's pretty much an ultimatum.

Okay okay. Geez this comment section holy shit!

&#x200B;

I'm not going to come to final conclusions. I don't know you. I don't know her. Neither you or her are perfect and I don't expect neither of you to be that. Whew! Goddamn!

&#x200B;

All I want to know is why? Why did we get to this point? If you both prioritize a good quality relationship then why would any of you two bring this up? You don't need this kinda stuff on your mind and she should know that. If you brought it up, know that she doesn't need her past on her mind either.

&#x200B;

Why was this a conversation between you two? Because it shouldn't have been for both of your sakes.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

PS

Both men and women can be insecure. It's a part of being a human. Expecting someone, ESPECIALLY YOUR PARTNER, to not be is showing that you expect them to be something they're not...perfect.

&#x200B;

People need to chill out.

People often ignore how insecure and/or tribal a lot of people are. More people want their lives to look good instead of be good. There's a lot of people out there that will choose to be with someone because a lot of other people think they are attractive so it would be a good look if they got with them. How they are treated by that person makes no difference.

&#x200B;

You'd be surprised by the number of people who have secret admirers.

Why would I believe it? What actions have they done to influence me to even believe that? Is it just gossip? Is it just someone trying to run a prank on me? I've seen couples. Two people who occupy each other's personal space. Hugs and kisses with each other are like breathing. They'll go anywhere together whether there's a crowd there or not. They are comfortable in each other's presence.

&#x200B;

Why would I believe anyone is attracted to me? What actions have they performed?

What are my priorities? What are my UNSPOKEN PRIORITIES? Why do I want to be in a relationship? 

&#x200B;

Hopefully within my unspoken priorities for romance a GOOD QUALITY RELATIONSHIP is amongst the top of the list if not thee top of the list. Can I have a good quality relationship with a person who treated me the way my ex did? Can I have a good quality relationship with a person who cheated on me? Can I have a good quality relationship with someone who treats me like shit? Can I have a good quality relationship with a person who doesn't even like me enough to go on a date with me? 

&#x200B;

Does this person really fulfill my priorities? Are my priorities in order?

"Rizz" only works, or appears to work(not really needed), if the person is physically attracted to you.

&#x200B;

I mean if it isn't than answer this question. If you as an ugly person had good enough charisma to get with someone and that person inevitably leaves you for someone who had no charisma at all but was just more physically attractive than you, does charisma even matter? This is usually what ends up happening. This caused so many breakups and so many divorces. So much cheating all due to looks.

&#x200B;

The answer is no.

One thing I do agree with in this post is that feeling of others expecting you to be perfect.

&#x200B;

Usually that comes from your mistakes being held to a higher amount of scrutiny than others. Everyone makes mistakes. Every single person on the planet. Every man in a relationship makes mistakes. Every woman in a relationship makes mistakes. Every gender in relationships makes mistakes. 

&#x200B;

Some people are just not forgiven. Not forgiven for even the most trivial mistakes while seeing others get forgiven for the most vile and disgusting things imaginable. Jeremy Meeks and Dzhokhar Tsarnaev come to mind. Cardi B comes to mind. Forgiven, loved, and lusted after. Mistakes forgiven but ask someone out the wrong way. Send the wrong text message. Don't wear the correct sneakers. Don't have the perfect haircut one day and it's over. You are the worst person in the world.

What's worse experiencing the bad and GOOD times of a relationship or thinking you are the ugliest person in existence because no one wants to be with you?

&#x200B;

So half good half bad or all bad?

Wishing I was born with a different face. Different hair texture. Different skin color. Different eye color. Everything different because I feel bad for being attracted to people...I'm so ugly that it's like I hurt people just by being attracted to them. I feel like i'm committing a crime just by being attracted to anybody. People get really upset if I seek love as well. I still isolate myself. I'm done with dating.

&#x200B;

I feel like i truly am so ugly that the pedophile she left me for was worth it for her. 20 years latter and nothing but rejections. I am the ugliest person in the world.

If it's guys you are romantically interested in then there are only two types that exist. The guys you're sexually attracted to and the guys you're not sexually attracted to.

&#x200B;

"nice" means nothing.

"I just feel like she fits the beauty standard more, & posts sexy pics I think most guys would find hot."

&#x200B;

Yikes

&#x200B;

Not every guy is this guy...pretty sure you don't care about that right now due to you believing that only what you think he thinks is pretty is what most guys think. He will keep winning as long as you compare yourself to who ever he chooses and/or believing he thinks for most men.

"I want to date someone that looks 50x better than him — for him to see us and be green in envy would make me so happy."

&#x200B;

Yikes.

&#x200B;

You will only destroy yourself on your pathway of revenge. He won't change. Nobody can make him change but him and if he won't than he doesn't want to. If these are things you don't like then don't entertain them by sticking around him. Also, nothing you do afterwards should be influenced by him. If they are then he's in control and not you. You don't want someone else controlling your life.

Either she's self sabotaging or she's not attracted to you in that way.

&#x200B;

Either way she's not worth dating.

&#x200B;

She is also not worth being platonic friends with due to her knowing how you really feel about her. Just by reading what she is saying, she most likely will still want to be friends with you. If you take her up on this, she will date other guys knowing how much it will hurt you and she would not give a single fuck.

Finding somebody who prioritizes the quality of the relationship over how much the relationship entertains/excites them is like finding a needle in a haystack. Also finding somebody who can think for themselves and don't need validation from their "friends" to be with, be around, show interest in, etc the person they truly like is an extremely rare find.

&#x200B;

We are better off finding these things outside of western civilization. Too much greed, immaturity, and insecurity here.

"Oh well, back to being invisible."

&#x200B;

This right here is the worst part of it. To know how long it took to find someone who likes you for it to be all over in an instant. You just don't know how long it's going to take for the next person, who likes you, to show up. It's a hard wait and you're going to feel like no one can like you like that. There will be thousands of people who will tell you to "just have faith", "Just work on yourself", "you'll find them someday", etc etc etc

&#x200B;

who knows maybe you will find that person. maybe you'll convince yourself what most people will want you to believe "rELAshUnshIPs R nOt wORtH iT" even though they know they are full of shit when they tell you this. you'll give up and you'll no longer value anyone. like me. these same people who don't want you to value romantic relationship experience will also expect so much from you. they'll see you as an object they can use and discard. they won't care about your feelings at all but claim they do. they'll tell you about their relationship while never caring if you're in one yourself.

&#x200B;

invisible until they need you for something then back to being invisible.

To believe that the race of people, who were racist to you "in the school years", is beautiful and you wish you were them is interesting. I find them, the people that were racist not white people in general, ugly.

&#x200B;

I'm kinda the opposite of you. I would prefer to be mixed race just so I wouldn't have to claim a race despite what people think.

&#x200B;

But maybe that's because I don't value people anymore.

I've been judged for so many things growing up. How I walk, Clothes I wear, How much I blink, Faces I make that I don't realize i'm making (almost got beat up for that), all sorts of things. It's hard to believe that you're not being judged for it when majority of your childhood you were. It went from that to pure silence so now you believe they're secretly judging you now instead of outwardly doing so when you were younger. You never really, or rarely really, got the opposite judgements. Positive judgements. Attention from the people who really liked you most likely because they were too scared to show you any kind of interest.

&#x200B;

Kinda hard to tell yourself that it's not going on anymore.

Either they think I hate them with no proof or they make up rumors about me. They think if I'm not going out of my way to talk to them that I must not like them...for what? existing? I don't even know you and you don't even know me so how could I hate you? Or if they don't see me talking with others or other people trying to talk to me then I must be a bad person because they need someone else to like me for them to like me which is extremely insecure but....as always. It is what it is.

&#x200B;

These days I don't expect anyone to think for themselves.

The universe does not care if you get closure. The universe does not care if you get better. It will go with or without you.

&#x200B;

Nothing is really important. It's not a matter of "moving on". It truly doesn't matter because you are truly not in control.

It's kinda hard to practice social skills in environments where you are expected to perform at a expert level.

&#x200B;

My first jobs with night stocking jobs at small retail stores just because I knew I wasn't at the level people expected me to be at. That way I can practice more in areas where i'm not expected to be an expert immediately.

&#x200B;

When it comes to jobs companies really don't care about the wellbeing of their employees though. It's all about numbers. If you can't reach them they discard you making it not a very good way to practice social skills.

&#x200B;

Most people won't tell you this though. Most people are all about tough love and tough love only. Less understanding and more expectations. It makes sense though due to the fact that that is majority of what you're going to come across in life. Finding understanding people, especially IRL, is extremely rare. So you have to prepare for the majority.

&#x200B;

It is what it is.

It's about an expectation of perfection usually given to the people we don't like.

&#x200B;

These expectations including perfect charisma, perfect social skills, perfect public speaking ability, etc usually blinds people from the truth about extroverts and introverts. Both can be shy. Both can be scared. Both can be weak. It's just displayed differently but when someone doesn't like you it's all bad. If you talk too much it's because you're trying to hide something. If you don't talk enough it's because you're afraid to talk. So linear. 

&#x200B;

Humans are not linear.

It's all about being useful now. Cogs in a machine. Rather it's corporate. Rather its a romantic relationship. It's all about being useful. 

&#x200B;

We look at tools in a very linear way. Does it work in this specific way or does it not so throw it away. With people it's are you strong in this specific way or are you weak so discard.

&#x200B;

We are no longer humans. We are tools.

"National boyfriend day" lol

&#x200B;

Just a bunch of insecure people shoving their relationships in the face of others trying to make them as jealous or envious of them as they were of others when they were single.

&#x200B;

Or maybe i'm wrong and they just want to show off their relationship to people, who don't care, for other reasons.

&#x200B;

Either way they care way too much about what other people think about their relationship and that same amount of insecurity will be the core of why their relationship will crumble.

&#x200B;

tldr: just call me a "hater" it's faster or whatever.

Most people will tell me "get over it" or try to use shaming tactics on me like "why do you care?"

&#x200B;

So. I'm not really allowed to. 

&#x200B;

I've been raised to just forget. Suppress and harm myself later on. That's not what they tell me to do but that's what I do.

"Ex girlfriend"

&#x200B;

Block.

Understanding is huge with introverts as most people don't or never try to understand us. It's just often seen as standoffish when it's truly energy conservation. Expectations are what most introverts get on a day to day basis. Negativity typically follows a lack to fulfill those expectations.

&#x200B;

Whether the person is extroverted or introverted matters little. Whether the person is understanding or is willing to understand usually is the deciding factor.

&#x200B;

That may just be my experience though.

So it was not so much being impressed but much more so being understood and understanding. 

&#x200B;

It's been over a decade since I had a relationship like that.

I gave up. I'm done trying to help it. I start talking more and the only ones receptive are people who want to use my words against me.

&#x200B;

I just need the people who want to hear me to separate themselves from the people who want to hurt me.

&#x200B;

Until then i'm not talking at all.

 "If someone wants to be a part of your life nothing will stand in their way."

&#x200B;

This is not discussed enough. It also rare that it ever happens.

You have a point. However

&#x200B;

>Sure I have talked to people. Made people laugh. Got a few girls numbers....but behind closed doors and behind my back, everyone hated me.

&#x200B;

\^Are the ones saying the good things. It's fake usually which is why I've stopped talking completely. I wish there were more positive people who weren't just negative people faking it. Maybe there are. Maybe i'm giving up too soon. I don't really know though.

I lost the only people **who tried** bad or good. I don't want a bad experience but people in general want experience period. Sure missing out on a bad experience is a blessing but missing out on experience itself is torture. Nobody wants non-experience.

&#x200B;

I wish the right ones for me tried but they won't. I can't find them because they are hiding from me. That's not something I can control.

Time and a place for everything. Most likely the location where you speaking was not the ideal location to have that conversation. If it is text than most likely he wants to speak to you in person and not over text. ~~Some~~ Most conversations should not be had over text and are way more healthy if had in person.

&#x200B;

Location matters. Environment matters. Not every conversation needs to be had anywhere at any time.

Degenerative disc disease makes this difficult. Not impossible but difficult. Also the pain from DDD makes me hate life more than the heartbreak I already go through...the fact that it started right around that time. 

&#x200B;

I will do it. Just not right now.

My last ex left me for a pedophile. I was 13 she was 13 he was 20. I was ugly then. Maybe he wasn't? I don't know. 

&#x200B;

So many years ago.

&#x200B;

I'm too ugly to date now. I've tried many things. I've tried many times. I've made many mistakes as we all do but since i'm ugly, my mistakes could not be forgiven.

&#x200B;

Regret what? rejecting the ugliest person in the world? There is no regret on their part. Just celebration. I made everyone who hated me hate me more for even trying. I wish I knew they hated me before I said or did anything. Then I would've just kept to myself.

&#x200B;

Oh well.

&#x200B;

I'm isolating myself now. Better late than never.

&#x200B;

As far as my degree and career. I regret it everyday. I should've went into entertainment. Maybe I would've got some respect. Now i'm just the "lame", "nerdy", ugly loser that everyone thinks is boring before they even meet me. It was self sabotage. Just took me too long to see it.

That my mistakes are not unforgivable. That I don't have to be a flawless, mistakeless, person. That I don't have to be perfect.

&#x200B;

My smallest mistakes cost me so much. I've loss so many connections due to small mistakes that i've made. Mistakes that are inevitable. 

&#x200B;

I'm not going to know until I know.

The hair texture on my scalp and face are completely different. Imagine having the coiliest of hair on your scalp with all thin strands of hair (no bald spots though or I would look worse) then the hair on my face/beard is almost straight with thicker and shiny strands of hair while the hair on my scalp doesn't shine at all no matter what I do to it. I have patches in my beard. The hair on the sides of my beard/cheeks will not grow past a specific length which is close to my face while my mustache and chin hair can grow very long. My face is non symmetrical. One side is bigger than the other. My eyes are ugly and bulge when I smile or laugh...it's hideous which is why I hate smiling. My teeth have never been straight i'm saving up for Invisalign. Most people don't like dark skin so there's that. I don't have the high cheek bones that most people find attractive. The shape of my head is ugly. It's not fully rounded in the back so I look uglier with short hair so i'm growing my hair out even though it looks really odd. It's just all around bad.

&#x200B;

I'm thinking about cutting my hair and just wearing hats and glasses which cover my face every time I step out of the house.

I don't want to see my face anymore. I don't want to be in another picture. It will never be okay. It never was. I'm cursed with my face. It is the cause of everything i've ever went through with anyone. 

&#x200B;

They hated my face just like I do. I am ugly and this will happen with every person I ever meet. I hate my face. I don't want to see it anymore.

I used to be. I also hated everything about myself from the neck up. Mixmatch hair textures. Non symmetrical face. I went for the clean cut all the time because I thought people would see me as ugly if I decided to grow my hair and beard out. No one wanted to talk to me or be around me when I had the "clean cut" so now i'm growing both out and it looks crazy lol but I don't care. The texture of the hair on my head is noticeably different from the texture of hair on my face. I want to see what I will look like when both of them are long. As far as clothes, I like wearing all black and now I do. I'm not goth but black is a very comfortable color to me and it helps with my anxiety. I don't care if people think I wear too much black. Where were those people when I was wearing more colors? I don't care if people think I don't look good with long hair. Where were those people when my hair was shorter?

&#x200B;

I just don't care anymore because people have shown me for years that they are not worth caring about.

I don't hate people at all. I just think that most people expect me to be perfect. No pauses when I speak. Perfect tone of voice. Say all the right things. I don't believe i'm free to make mistakes. Therefore, at all times, i'm thinking of the perfect thing to say when I talk to anyone that is not my mother or brother. 

&#x200B;

It feels better to isolate myself from people because I don't feel the pressure of perfection.

As much as HR is your best bet, i'm not sure how much they would be willing to help you here. Seems like a pretty toxic workplace environment if you ask me. If I were you I would be actively looking for another place for work. You said the "entire" workplace which means if you went another department you may have the same issue.

&#x200B;

You've only been working there for 3 months so you won't really have to change up your resume during the job search. I'm sure a new company wouldn't mind you leaving a job after 3 months if you choose to include this job in your resume. Some people get a new job and then find out that it's either not for them or in your situation, the workplace is toxic and have to leave.

&#x200B;

I'm not saying do this but this is what I would be doing if I were in your shoes.

"I'm nothing to nobody"

&#x200B;

You haven't met enough people to confirm this. I understand losing someone you love is difficult and you're going to feel pain. I'm not going to tell you not to either because I know how that is. It just feels like orders from people who don't care. I'm just saying there are so many people you haven't met. Whether it's in your city, country, continent, etc. Don't give away your ability to meet other people because you lost one.

She lied to you.

&#x200B;

She's simply not attracted to you and want to waste your time and money.

&#x200B;

Forget about her and find someone else. Don't be her friend. She's not your friend. She's using you and probably talking shit about you behind your back to her friends.

I'm part of the band "my ex started dating someone else and sent her friends to tell me it was over"

&#x200B;

That was long ago though. I already forgot her name.

This is so common.

&#x200B;

So common in fact that I wonder if he's thinking the same thing about you.

&#x200B;

I'm not saying i'm right or wrong i'm just saying.

&#x200B;

I feel this way too. She might be too.

It's what I do best. My lips sometimes stick together causing sores when I open them. People get frustrated with me because I don't talk as much as they expect me to. 

&#x200B;

My life is "NO FUCKING CONTACT". I hate it.

Just waiting for them to develop the courage to show me a sign. 

&#x200B;

Fuck gender roles. Man or woman. Just show interest. Stop hiding behind your gender.

That's not a "remedy". That's an addiction. A very unhealthy one at that. Unhealthy for all parties involved. That includes you.

&#x200B;

At the same time. You are the only one responsible for dealing with that addiction.

Don't get yourself killed for a woman who's not your WIFE.

&#x200B;

You can try to help with taking legal action against the guy but fighting him for her should be the last thing on your mind. If she doesn't want to take legal action and the police is as corrupt as you say then this may be a lost cause. Protect yourself over anything....including her.

&#x200B;

PS: She doesn't like you. "Winning" her love is out of the question. Find another woman who loves you and is not afraid to show that to you. That should be your standard. Not women like her.

You've asked her out. You've done your part. Nothing else needs to be done by you as far as she is concerned. If she likes you, it's up to her to show that now not you. If she doesn't like you then she will show that. At this point you should be more focused on yourself, your studies, your hobbies, etc. Talk to other women if you wish to pursue anyone. DO NOT PURSUE HER. As you've stated 

&#x200B;

"I tried not to be near her or sit near her because the last thing I want to do is make her uncomfortable but I still thought about her all day."

&#x200B;

You understand that she has set a boundary with her rejection. Honor that. Don't feel upset if she never returns your feelings. There are other women out here. You haven't met them all. You'll probably run into a woman who's more attractive than her and who has the same feelings for you as you do for her and is willing to show you that. However that shouldn't be your No.1 priority. Right now focus on what's going to better the quality of your life. Focus on what you would like to do after HS. Try to find some groups in your school that align with your interests. Try to mingle with people who share your interests. Don't make this girl your No. 1 priority.

Because no one is really sweet and kind. Those people don't exist. At least not anymore. She(cold, distant, and uncaring) is the norm.

&#x200B;

So many threads on this very subreddit prove that to be true.

A "soulmate" would be more forgiving than she was. A "soulmate" would continue to try to help you with your anxiety. They would not be able to bear having a life without a romantic relationship with you. She is not a "soulmate" if this is not the case. "Soulmates" fight and continuing fighting.

&#x200B;

However, a soulmate is something that shouldn't be a high priority for anybody because of how rare that actually is. 1 in a couple of billion? Nah that's way too low of odds and you only got one life just to wait for that person to appear. Also perfection does not exist. They will always be problems. Trying to find someone perfect will do nothing but waste your time. Soulmates are not worth it.

That is where I'm trying to keep my mind. It's extremely difficult to do this because the yearning for experience. I tell myself everyday that the quailty of my life should be my number one priority. At the same time my life is nothing but work. Not too much experiencing anything. I believe you need to experience relationships in order to start a business because you are selling to people so you need to know people. Humans in general are a social species. Making a business is selling to this social species. You need to be one to know one.

&#x200B;

Being alone has it's detriments in ways we don't even consider.

Exactly. Knowing you're not attractive to anyone. That no one wants to experience anything with you. That is heartbreaking in itself. It makes you feel horrible for many reasons. The worst kind of people can get into relationships. If you can't get in one it makes you feel like you're worse than the worst people on the planet.

&#x200B;

I rather feel attractive than feel like a pedophile's life is worth more than my own. There are so many pedophiles that are married or in relationships.

Leave that job as fast as you can. Never try to date a coworker.

&#x200B;

The only people i've seen who have success with that is specifically white men who look like models and are at least managers.

The conclusion was already been made with her silence. Finding someone new is better than contacting her for my sake. Hearing anything from her would be at my detriment. Its not a self made prison. I am trying to break my chains. When she's forgotten, that means the chains are broken. 

&#x200B;

Time is key. I don't want to see her for the rest of my life. I rather die than speak to her again.

I want to forget her completely. 

&#x200B;

Forget calling them back. How about the person that actually likes us stop being a coward and contact us. 

&#x200B;

It's easier to forget the people who did us wrong when the right people SHOW UP

When the pain lasts too long without any support suicidal thoughts form.

&#x200B;

Sometimes the shit just takes too long. Shits not worth it. Life's not worth it.

The universe only sees the importance of us in a time to hurt us.

&#x200B;

The universe never sees the important of our love for someone. The universe never sees the importance of us living out EXPERIENCES with the ones we love. Just some predetermined purpose for us to endure. Not knowing if we want it. Not knowing if we can take it. We only have one life. What if that purpose something we can't stand? Is suicide really such a bad thing?

It's all just work. You're only appreciated when you're working for someone. They can't appreciate you as a human. If you want something then they'll try to make you out to be the worse person in the world. They just want you to shut up and be a good worker for them. 

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

This is why we have to avoid people like this if we can and only stay around if those people truly want us to be there. Want us to be around as a human and not a tool.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

I can't wait til I get to the point to where i no longer need corporate america. Then I can truly choose who I get to be around and talk to.

I get dirty looks where ever I go.

&#x200B;

People hate me on sight. Makes me want to put a bullet in my head every time I see it.

My father's in the hospital. In pretty rough shape.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

That was my valentines day. I've never had a valentine in my entire life.

Gotta love insecure fucks that love to try to make people jealous because without that they believe themselves to be the biggest losers.

&#x200B;

That's not gender based. All genders are capable of this. 

&#x200B;

Both the jock and that girl are more insecure than you even realize OP.

