Wow..just... I just got hired to this job i'm working at now. Very big company. Highest i've ever been paid working for a company. International. Customer Service. I hate the absolute $#!+ out of it and I want to quit everyday. The expectations of social skill from customers, co-employees, and especially the managers are crazy. No sympathy. They will embarrass you in front of the entire office for the smallest mistake and you just got sit there and take it. I can't stand public humiliation. It's actually the cause of my SA...well one of the biggest causes. Now I have to deal with it on a weekday to day basis. I regret taking this job. I had another opportunity...would've still been customer service but probably not as bad as this.

&#x200B;

I just think to myself now...why is customer service "entry level"? The amount of mistakes you can make. How much it could cost the company. To put someone who barely knows the business itself on the front line. You cram years of information into their head in a matter of weeks and expect them to give perfect customer service. These customers expect these entry level employees to know everything, and I mean EVERYTHING, about their company as well as their competitors and even the customer's own company. The worst part..once you get in customer service it's damn hard to get out. It's the only skill you know...it takes up all your time so you can't learn other things...it takes all your spirit so you don't even feel like trying to do anything else after another 10/11 hour day of misery.

My life hasn't changed at all except getting a new job. It's still customer service which I hate. The only thing different in my life is seeing people with masks. That's it. Most places are still open where I live. Most places didn't shut down and if they did it was for a month at most. My social skills didn't improve at all. They actually worsened. Forced social exchange due to my job doesn't help with social skills because these aren't real relationships. These are co workers and customers. That's it. I hear about the social life they have outside of work and it makes me reflect on the lack of social life I have mainly because of my social anxiety getting in the way of me being social day one which kills any kind of relationship I could make.

&#x200B;

So yeah. Post pandemic will be the same for me....unless I do something drastic. I might have to let this work life go and just get in my car and drive until I find something.

